<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Finding the probability of intersection and union of two events and their complements</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>\(A\) and \(B\) are two events and \(P(A) ={@p_a@},  P(B) ={@p_b@}\) and \(P(A\cap B)={@p_anb@}\)</p>
<p>\(\text{Find:}\)</p>
<p>(a) \(P(A\cup B)=\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]][[feedback:prt1]]</p>
<p>(b) \(P(B^C)=\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]][[feedback:prt2]]</p>
<p>(c) \(P(A\cap B^C)=\) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]][[feedback:prt3]]</p>
<p>(d) \(P(A\cup B^C)=\) [[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]][[feedback:prt4]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Worked out solution</p>

<p>(a) Recall that for any two sets \(X\) and \(Y\), \(P(X\cup Y)=P(X)+P(Y)-P(X\cap Y)\)
Therefore;
 \(P(A\cup B) = P(A) + P(B) – P(A\cap B) = {@p_a@}+{@p_b@}-{@p_anb@}={@ta1@}\)</p>

<p>(b) For any set \(X\), its complement \(X^C\) represents all elements, not in \(X\) but are within the probability space and \(P(X)+P(X)^C=1\). Therefore;
 \( P(B^C) = P(S)-P(B)\)</p>
<p>\(\text{The probability of sample space is always 1}\)</p>
<p>OR \(1-P(B) = 1-{@p_b@} = {@ta2@}\)</p>

<p>(c) Recall, for any two sets \(X\) and \(Y\), elements not in \(X\) and are in \(Y\) can be represented as \(Y\cap X^C\). Therefore;
\( P(A\cap B^C) = P(A) – P(A\cap B) = {@p_a@}-{@p_anb@}={@ta3@}\)</p>

<p>(d) Recall, for any two sets \(X\) & \(Y\), elements in \(X\) are also in \(Y^C\) and can represented as \(X\cup Y^C\) Therefore;
 \(P(A\cup B^C) =  P(A) + P(A\cup B)^C = {@p_a@}+{@p_not@} = {@ta4@}\) </p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
